WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:02.628
♪♪

00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:04.671
(Crowd noise)

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.673
(Whistle blows)

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:18.977
(Crowd noise)

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:20.145
(Knocking on door)

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:21.146
Howdy, y'all.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:22.147
(All)
Ted!

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:24.066
What do you say to a cocktail,
Coach Lasso?

00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:27.152
Oh, the same thing I'd say to
Diane Sawyer, if she ever asked
me out on a date. Yes, please.

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:28.153
Hahaha.

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:29.404
♪♪

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:33.283
Announcer:
Live from the Dog track, it's
Richmond with eight straight ties.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:35.410
How many more matches
before you hit the panic button?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.247
There's two buttons I never like
hitting. That's panic and
snooze.

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:39.289
♪♪

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:40.415
Ted:
I don't care what our record is.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:43.794
It's all about believing that
everything is going to work out
in the end. Exactly as it's suppose to.

00:00:43.794 --> 00:00:47.714
Ted:
Isn't the idea of "never give
up" one of them things we always talk about in sports?

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.341
Ted:
And shouldn't that apply to
people too?

00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.718
It's a beautiful metaphor for
many of life's journeys.

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:55.055
♪♪

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.890
The teams just a little unlucky,
that's all.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.058
♪♪

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.602
I think we should bring in
a sports psychologist.

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:02.604
Brought you a little, somethin'
somethin' for your first day of
work here.

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:05.440
I don't eat sugar...

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.818
Really? I've never met someone
who doesn't eat sugar.

00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:10.654
Only heard about them, and they
all live in this godless place
called Santa Monica.

00:01:10.654 --> 00:01:11.655
♪ Sing it ♪

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.116
♪ We will, we Will ♪

00:01:14.116 --> 00:01:15.200
(Crowd cheers)

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.493
♪ Rock you ♪

00:01:16.493 --> 00:01:18.704
You gotta fever for the flavor
of little girl talk, don't you?

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:20.580
This chap I've been seeing,
John.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.581
Stamos?

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:24.042
No. His names John
Wingsnight.

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.712
Like at a sports bar, like
"Monday night's wings night,
down at PJ Flats".

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:27.838
Would you please stop?

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:31.008
Rule number 1. Even though it's
called girl talk, sometimes it
needs to be more like,

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:32.217
Girl, listen.

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:36.346
♪ We will, we will rock you ♪

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:40.475
♪ We will, we will rock you ♪

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:42.060
♪♪

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.228
What's Ted doing?

00:01:43.228 --> 00:01:44.354
Probably home sick.

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:46.064
Closest thing he can find to a
Dodge Ram.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:47.065
Woohoo!

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:49.860
♪♪

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.279
Back home, if a team was playing
poorly, we don't call them
unlucky.

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:53.280
What do we call them, Coach?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.323
New York Jets.

00:01:54.323 --> 00:01:56.742
♪♪

